# Caps every account engine and viewer together, leaving about 6 GB of the 12 GB server for the
# gateway, NGINX, SiYuan, sing-box and the system. Measured engine peaks: median 363M, p90 627M,
# max 912M; viewers up to 84M. Seven accounts at their p90 need about 4.8 GB; all seven at their
# worst-ever peak (about 6.8 GB) would hit the cap, where the kernel kills only the largest process
# in this slice.
# No MemoryHigh or systemd-oomd here: MemoryHigh only stalls the growing engine, and on
# systemd 255 oomd's per-unit kill failed and fell back to killing every unit in the slice.
[Unit]
Description=GoodMorning account services

[Slice]
MemoryMax=6G
MemorySwapMax=0
